{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In pastures</b> — the meaning is that He will find grass, and there will be a nearby pasture there, so that the sheep will not weary on the mountains when it lies down." "<b>By waters</b> — He mentioned the waters." "And the meaning of <b>מנוחות</b> (resting waters) — the opposite of a rushing stream."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:20.480226183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}